=== ISOLATION RESULT (repro_01b_lineage_warm_append.py) ===
10/10 iterations clean when LineageStore is pre-constructed (single process,
no race) BEFORE spawning 12 concurrent writer processes doing append() only.
jsonl raw line count: 2400/2400 and sqlite row count: 2400/2400 on all 10 runs.
Zero "database is locked" errors.

CONCLUSION: the race is confined to the COLD-START constructor path
(_init_db() -> _connect() -> PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL on a not-yet-existing
or freshly-created file), not to steady-state concurrent append() calls
against an already-WAL-mode-established file. Commit 14bf8b1's busy_timeout
fix is effective for its actual target (concurrent writers appending to an
established WAL db) but does NOT cover concurrent first-time construction
of the store, which remains a live, unhandled crash/data-loss path.
